.TH AGENT-WORKFLOW-EVIDENCE 1 "2026-08-02" "agent-workflow 0.7.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-workflow-evidence \- append-only supplemental interpretation of sealed run evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-workflow evidence repair
.BI --source-run " SESSION"
.BI --source-receipt " SHA256"
.BI --artifact " RELATIVE_PATH"
.RI [ --adapter " completion-normalize-v1" ]
.BI --output-run " REPAIR_ID"
.BI --actor " ACTOR"
.br
.B agent-workflow evidence verify
.I REPAIR_ID
.br
.B agent-workflow evidence list
.RI [ --source-run " SESSION" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The evidence command records a deterministic supplemental interpretation without editing a sealed historical run. Each repair binds the exact source session, final-receipt SHA-256, sealed artifact path, and artifact SHA-256. Source evidence is fingerprinted before and after generation. Repair artifacts and their receipt are stored separately under the state root and made read-only.
.PP
A repair is evidence, not acceptance authority. It does not replace the original completion collection, lifecycle result, evaluation result, or ledger classification. Verified linkage is exposed in evaluation reports, ledger rows, and the SQLite repairs view while the original interpretation remains preserved.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B repair
Create one append-only repair. The repair identity is idempotent only for the same source receipt, artifact, digest, and adapter. Reusing it for different evidence fails.
.TP
.B verify
Rehash the repair receipt and artifacts, validate schemas and read-only modes, verify the adapter identity and canonical digest, and reverify the bound source final receipt.
.TP
.B list
List valid and invalid repair records, optionally filtered by source run.
.SH ADAPTER
.B completion-normalize-v1
may normalize only completion schema and session identity plus legacy review disposition/result encoding. It does not rewrite criteria, commands, command receipts, revisions, changed files, unresolved findings, ticket or pack identity, or usage. A legacy command string, missing receipt, or other substantive schema failure remains invalid.
.SH SAFETY
Absolute, parent-traversing, backslash, symlink, non-regular, hard-linked, writable, changed, or unsealed artifacts fail closed. The source final-receipt digest and source artifact digest must match exactly. Partial repair directories are removed on failed creation; a successful repair remains append-only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/agent-workflow/evidence-repairs/<repair-id>/
Separate supplemental evidence directory containing adapter.json, canonical-completion.json, evidence-repair.json, and repair-receipt.json.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-workflow (1),
.BR agent-workflow-index (1)
